kwExprT -- SEQ 579 (Tony, 2026-11-09): a keyword inside an expression refuses by name on the NEW road. Rows prefixed KE- (cure),
KC- (new-road controls), KO- (old-road controls, already loud, unmoved). Interpreted only.

TODAY, measured: on the new road a Keywords entry (if, while, do, for, print, else, this, ... -- the registry, not a list here)
anywhere in an expression fails ANYtoken (ruleActions.rtn:9, aCTionANYtoken: a keyWords field is not a token), so the statement
cannot match and STARt / FILe stop QUIETLY: the statement and every statement after it are dropped, exit 0, no word. A new-road
ACTION is loud already (its build fails; the old road's processCode reports). The old road is loud everywhere: ABANDONED at the
top level, `ERROR processCode ... parse failed` in an action.

THE CURE (new road only): KEYWORd, TOKEn's last alternative, lets the keyword reach EXPRESSIOn, which refuses it by name and ends
the statement. `qr = if qa; 1 else 2;` then refuses twice -- if, and else in the next statement `1 else 2;` -- because the first
`;` ends the statement. Keyword forms AS expressions stay unruled (the ; question, docs/ruleAsOperator.md R5).

Not run alone: pop.sh appends the row, print "NEXT", a sentinel; one process per row. Each row reads exit and sentinel; stdout
(lines joined by |); and a stderr summary -- the keywords refused by name, then ABANDONED and PARSEFAIL when those lines appear.

